Subject:&nbsp;Re: Pan-NOx Diesel Emissions Group Litigation [SIG-LIT-LIT.FID5824]
&nbsp;


Hi Alicia,




Thanks and understood. Is there a reason why Martyn (and the silks) should have input into what we advise our client committees?&nbsp;




While I appreciate the desire for the news to come from the firm (and I'm happy to work with the firm on this), I have a professional relationship with the client committee and I feel quite strongly that I am permitted to inform them myself, with the firm in
 copy, or on a call with others in attendance. I'm not intending on this being done in a manner to generate issues - the opposite in fact. I believe the news coming from me, and in advance of my leaving, will be much better received than them receiving an email
 from someone they have had no dealings with to say I've left the firm.&nbsp;&nbsp;




To the extent it is reassuring, the NOx committees are significantly more passive than I understand others, so I cannot see the news generating real issues, but I do feel strongly about me being the one to deliver the news.&nbsp;




Thanks,






























​​​​































Michael&nbsp;Burke











(He/Him)

















