&nbsp;

Thanks for this Anna.

&nbsp;

I have not reviewed it to make comments (I don't think I am currently best suited to!) but my only observation is that at various&nbsp; points there is a discussion of &quot;the pan-nox
 team&quot;. The letter also says &quot;Should any material development arise that affect our ability to progress the litigation in accordance with the Court’s directions, we would notify the parties and the Court as appropriate.&quot;

&nbsp;

The Ds have already raised issue with the fact that they found out Pete was leaving in the press. Is there any thought to be given to using this letter as a flag that the
 other case leads in the lead cases are also due to leave? I can already imagine the howls from the Ds if nothing is said to them now and then they are later told, and they will no doubt ask &quot;why didn't you tell us then&quot;

&nbsp;

For clarity - I am not advocating for it at this point, I'm just wondering if it was considered (albeit if they do wish to put it in, I imagine the case leads would need
 to be consulted on it - as the letter recognises).&nbsp;

&nbsp;

I am due to inform my client committee of this FYI.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Thanks,

































