y. For example, if there was a £2m claim on the Ford top-up but all the other matters recovered proceeds, these proceeds would be applied to that £2m loss to make Toremis whole. We see this structure being advantageous to PG as: i.) overall the cost of insurance will be reduced and ii.) all matters will be covered – Toremis would not cherry-pick the strongest matters and only offer insurance against these. Separately Toremis would need to be added to the individual PDs in this matter which is the usual process when an excess layer is added. They would slot into the equivalent position of a 2nd/3rd/4th layer insurer (as applicable).Toremis are aware of the pre-existing cross-collateralisation provisions (Nathan Hull was head of ATE at VALE when these documents were put in place). They are comfortable with the fact that they would sit below these (as to do otherwise would need to unwind the provisions that are in place).@Anna Varga @Matt Hunt,@Matthew Newbould Re the merits call later – Toremis have no particular queries the case leads would need to be aware of. It will essentially be fleshing out the bullet-point queries sent to Counsel (below) / giving a “state of the nation” walk-through of the merits of the matter, similar to the call conducted with the existing insurers ahead of the PDD trial.&nbsp;Confirming, at a high level, that, with the benefit of having now reviewed the expert and factual evidence (and the detailed legal position taken by the defendants) the merits remain at least as good as the original assessments (including confirming what the relevant percentage assessment is for each of the defendants).Confirming the position on the merits in relation to: (1) whether each of the defendants' vehicles contained unlawful defeat devices; (2) whether there are any viable article 5 defences available to the defendants; and (3) to the extent separate to (1) and (2), the position on the existence of a breach of statutory duty and/or a breach of contract.&nbsp;