Please find below latest developments regarding NOx and responses to Ignite’s queries.
&nbsp;
Lead Solicitor
&nbsp;
The Firm has in consultation with the other Lead Solicitor and subject to the Court’s approval
 decided to step down temporarily as Lead Solicitor in the lead cases.&nbsp; This will obviate any attempt by the Defendants to distract the proceedings tactically by (unmerited) references to our personnel/legal team changes.&nbsp; The firm remains a fully active member
 of the Steering Committee, and is in the process of agreeing mechanisms whereby it can continue work on the matter in substantive terms. We do not anticipate material financial impact
on the conduct of the proceedings.
We address Ignite’s questions and the questions about Tom Goodhead in your email of today below.

&nbsp;
Response to insurer queries

&nbsp;


Key Personal/Lead Lawyers - per the verbal request can the lead lawyers per NOx manufacturer and for the BHP matter be detailed to us please?&nbsp;

The board of directors now comprises Alicia Alinia, Howard Morris, and Joseph Moreno as directors of both the Parent
 and the Firm (the “Board”). Thomas Goodhead has now left both as CEO and Director of the Firm.&nbsp; The Board is responsible for the overall management of the Firm, and each member of the Board has statutory duties to exercise independent judgment in accordance
 with the Companies Act 2006.
The Board appointments demonstrate that Pogust Goodhead is being run by an extremely experienced and committed team
 of independent, regulated, legal professionals. Each of the Board members is regulated by the SRA and qualified to practice in England &amp; Wales.
Following Pete’s departure, Anna Varga, whom you have met, has taken the lead on Mercedes and Vauxhall cases and is
 overall supervisor for the remaining NOx cases. Working closely with our case leads, Anna will ensure a smooth transition and maintain consistency in how the cases are managed. [For BHP our case leads are
 Guy Robson and Faranak Ghajavand].
&nbsp;
Additionally, we are delighted to have engaged one of the market’s
 leading litigation practices [Pallas Partners], to work alongside us on the emissions cases providing access to senior level strategic legal advice for liability and quantum workstreams.
Craig Shuttleworth (Kastle Solicitors and previously Head of Litigation at Jones Day), who has decades of litigation experience is also joining us as a strategic
 advisor on emissions. Craig has been working with the firm supporting BHP and other matters since 2023[, and will work to support teams across both the NOx and BHP matters].
&nbsp;
We want to reassure you that the cases continue to receive the level of expertise and attention required. Our retained
 barristers and partner firms remain fully engaged and unchanged, providing continuity and stability in external representation. Internally, the team continues to operate with the senior oversight and leadership necessary to progress the cases effectively.
 We are confident that this structure offers the strongest platform for achieving a successful outcome

We can confirm that Mr Burke has formally tendered his resignation with Pogust Goodhead and is currently working his notice period. We will liaise with the Defendants in those Litigations to advise them accordingly.
