Dear Defendants’ Solicitors,
As solicitors representing a group of 750,000 claimants in the NOx Litigations, we are constantly vigilant to ensure that we are acting in the best interests of our clients and to forward the
 efficient case management of this important litigation.
With that in mind, and in view of the various allegations that the Defendants have advanced, we have determined that our continued status as Lead Solicitors across the Lead Cases, and the focus
 put on us as a firm in this role, is causing unnecessary distractions, at least in the current moment, and threatening to imperil the trial. Therefore, we are writing to inform you of our intention in principle to resign as Lead Solicitors from the Lead Cases
 on a temporary basis for the duration of the liability trial. 
This should not be taken as acceptance that any of your recent criticisms about the Firm’s capacity to conduct this work in a responsible, compliant fashion are correct. We stand by our position
 in the letter to you dated 23 September 2025.
We shall continue to work diligently on behalf of our clients, and will remain as a member of the Mercedes Sterring Committee.&nbsp; We will also conduct the necessary trial work as authorised &nbsp;by
 the remaining Lead Solicitors and/or the Steering Committee (as the case may be), as explicitly authorised by the Court in the applicable Group Litigation Orders (the “GLOs”).
