ing, nor have we done anything, that would put us or you in breach of your regulatory or professional &nbsp;requirements. Everything we have done or are intending to do is with the best interests of our clients in mind. Second, regarding your future employment, we expect you to work till the end of your notice period, as contractually agreed. After that period, we understand from the Johnson Law Group that you intend to work there together with Pete Gallagher. We are comfortable for you to do so after the end of your notice period. Johnson Law Group have also confirmed to us that they are not expecting you to join them before the end of the trial. With that in mind, and given your dedication to working in the best interest of the clients, we ask that you work [four] extra days through until the end of the trial, being 19 December 2025. You would be paid your usual salary, and receive all benefits, through until this extended date. If you are agreeable to this arrangement, please could you confirm that to me. Both Pogust Goodhead and Johnson Law Group consider this arrangement will help ensure the clients of Pogust Goodhead (and other firms) are not prejudiced or detrimentally impacted moving forward.Third, it is important to clarify how the Agency Agreement will work – this should give you immediate comfort on the proposed approach.PG’s proposed role is exactly as envisaged in the Pan NOx Agency Agreement, which we have all been working under: PG will, as authorised by the Pan NOx Agency Agreement, act by authorisation of LD with respect to the Common Work delegated to it by LD.&nbsp; The Agency Agreement will enable PG to continue working on the liability trial and quantum workstream while you remain with us working your notice period. In terms of what will change practically, LD will be sole Lead Solicitor, which means that it will be responsible for final decisions in terms of matters such as filing and serving documents, or providing instructions to counsel. PG 