&nbsp;&nbsp;From: Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Date: Monday, 20 October 2025 at 09:49To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: ReportCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Morning Alicia, Anna and Raminder, &nbsp;We attach a draft response to the email below for your review. We also think that Clydes should review before it goes. &nbsp;Separately, if you have a whistleblower policy or any other policy for dealing with protected disclosures, you should see if it contains a required procedure for dealing with such disclosures, and ensue you follow it (for example, the response may need to come from a particular person). &nbsp;Please let us know if you have any comments or questions. &nbsp;Best regards, &nbsp;Xenia &nbsp;Xenia&nbsp;KalognomasAssociateT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1065|M:&nbsp;77&nbsp;0121&nbsp;8358E:&nbsp;&nbsp;xenia.kalognomas@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInPallas Partners LLP is a limited liability partnership registered in England with registered number OC437491, and is authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority of England and Wales (“SRA”) with SRA number 826251. A list of names of the members is available for inspection at our registered address at&nbsp;110 Bishopsgate, London, EC2N 4AY.&nbsp;The word “partner” denotes a member of&nbsp;Pallas Partners LLP&nbsp;or an employee or consultant with equivalent standing and qualifications.&nbsp;Pallas Partners (US) LLP is a limited liability partnership established in Delaware and registered in New York, located at 75 Rockefeller Plaza, New York, NY, 10019.&nbsp;Attorneys practicing law with Pallas Partners (US) LLP are admitted to practice in New York and their professional conduct is regulated by the New York Rules of Professional Conduct.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;This email (and any attachments) is confidential and may also be legally privileged and is intended solely for the use of the individual or entity addressed above. If you are not the intended recipient, please immediately notify the sender, then delete it from your system. You should not copy it or use it for any purpose, nor disclose its contents to any other person. Please also note that emails sent or received may be monitored to ensure compliance with the law and with our policies.&nbsp;Further regulatory information can be found in the Legal Notices which appear on our website at&nbsp;https://www.pallasllp.com/legal.​​​​From: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 17 October 2025 13:28To: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: Report&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOS​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Friday, October 17, 2025 1:22 pmTo:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Priyanka Gladson &lt;pgladson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Report &nbsp;Dear Board,&nbsp;We write further to the emails exchanged between Michael Burke, Sarah Bingham and Anna Varga dated 15 and 16 October 2025 as they relate to the Litigation Management Agreement (&quot;LMA&quot;)&nbsp;and Agency Agreement (&quot;AA&quot;). This email is intended to be a protected disclosure.&nbsp;&nbsp;As can be seen from the First Witness Statement of Alicia Alinia dated 30 September at paragraph 35.1 - she has confirmed (and verified with a statement of truth): &quot;For the avoidance of doubt, Gramercy has no control over the day-to-day management or decisions of the Firm or the Partner, and nor does Gramercy have any role in the conduct, control or management of the NOx Group Litigations.&quot;&nbsp;Further, at 35.3, it is confirmed that &quot;Its board of directors is entirely independent of Gramercy, and nothing in its financial arrangements inhibits the Firm from actively, and independently, pursuing the Proceedings in the best interests of its clients.&quot;&nbsp;On account of the email sent by Anna Varga on 16 October at 8.57AM in which she explicitly instructs Sarah Bingham to instruct Stewarts (who are retained by Gramercy - see email from Joshua Katz dated 13.05.2025 confirming this) to provide input into documents central to the NOx Litigation - the statement at 35.1 is now categorically untrue. Senior management has instructed a member of staff to engage with a firm which is instructed by Gramercy to review both Pan NOx and PG specific documents. This position therefore must be corrected to the Court and to the Defendants (and to the PG staff) where the firm have represented that Gramercy does not have input into the conduct of the&nbsp;Litigations (in&nbsp;the case of to the Court - with a signed statement of truth).&nbsp;&nbsp;With regard to 35.3 - see the email from Julian Chamberlayne on 9 September 2025 at 11.30 in which he confirms that &quot;I have now heard from Gramercy that, based on our review, they are content with you proceeding with the revised agency agreements&quot;&nbsp;. In circumstances where Stewarts, instructed by Gramercy, are reviewing and providing approval in respect of key NOx documents and requiring PG to await execution prior to their approval, it cannot be true to state that the Firm can independently pursue the Proceedings (and is in fact doing so) cannot be true.&nbsp;We completely understand that a litigation funder&nbsp;will have a legitimate interest in reviewing certain documents, and may quite properly wish to have input where those documents either (a) give rise to a financial liability on the funder, or (b) relate to compliance with the funding terms.We also acknowledge PG’s position under the funding arrangements in particular, the covenant requiring PG to obtain the funder’s prior approval before engaging any new law firm or barrister to whom PG grants a contingent interest. This requirement exists because such engagements could create a financial exposure that Gramercy may ultimately need to meet.However, the Pan-NOx Agency Agreement&nbsp;does not&nbsp;fall within that category. It does not create any contingent interests, nor does it involve any cost contribution obligations from the Non-Lead Firms. Its purpose is purely to define the principal–agent relationship&nbsp;between Pogust Goodhead (as Lead Solicitor) and the Non-Lead Firms, governing the conduct, management, strategy decisions and coordination of the litigation. In short, it enables PG to act independently as Lead Solicitor within the proceedings.Similarly, the Litigation Management Agreement is not a funding or liability document. Rather, it is an agreement between the Client Committee and Pogust Goodhead, setting out the instructions, authority and governance framework&nbsp;under which PG acts for the claimants within each GLO. It defines procedural and operational responsibilities, not financial exposure, and is an essential component of PG’s authority to manage the litigation.The level of control that Gramercy has sought to exercise over these documents &nbsp;which govern solicitor-client relationships, not funder obligations&nbsp; goes far beyond the usual parameters of a lender–borrower relationship. It represents an overreach into the conduct and management of the litigation itself, rather than oversight of financial risk. That distinction is fundamental, and Gramercy’s continued involvement in these matters strays beyond what is permissible for a funder maintaining a proper arm’s-length relationship with the litigation.It therefore&nbsp;appears that our collective position is that PG is&nbsp;now openly operating in a world where the funder of the firm has direct management/control of aspects of the litigation - and that control is on-going, despite representations&nbsp;to the contrary made to the Court, the Defendants and to the staff. This creates significant issues for the staff working on these Litigations both in our duties to our clients and to the clients of the other firms in our firm's role as Lead Solicitors.&nbsp;&nbsp;Can you please advise on the following:&nbsp;why representations have been made to the Court, Defendants and staff that Gramercy do not have any role in the conduct, control or management of the NOx Group Litigations when plainly - they do and continue to do so;whether the Board intends to update the Court as to the true position; andwhether the Board intends to inform the clients and other claimant firms of Gramercy's input into documents that have a direct bearing on costs and client instructions.&nbsp;We are continuing to consider this on-going issue as more information comes to light. All of our rights are reserved.&nbsp;&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael, Priyanka, Sarah&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344&nbsp;"}

