&nbsp;
Dear Michael,
&nbsp;
Thank you for your email and for the welcome back. I appreciate you keeping us informed about your fitness for work, and I have answered your questions below.
&nbsp;
Eligibility for Occupational Sick Pay (OSP)
I understand your concerns, and I appreciate the opportunity to clarify the firm’s position. Clause 13.4 of your contract states that eligibility for company sick pay is
“subject to… the Company’s Sickness Policy.” The Sickness Policy forms part of the contractual framework governing sickness absence and OSP, and the eligibility criteria contained in the Policy, including the requirement that an employee has not given
 notice to terminate their employment, therefore apply in full.
&nbsp;
For that reason, as you have given notice, you are not eligible for OSP during the notice period. This is a standard provision within the policy and has been applied consistently
 across the firm in all comparable circumstances.
&nbsp;
Return to work and IT access
If you become medically fit to return to work before 15 December, please let me know as soon as possible. In this instance, we would arrange for the IT team to reinstate your system access so that you can resume work and complete the handover required before
 your final day.
&nbsp;
Final pay
Your final pay will include:

SSP for the period of certified sickness absencePayment for your six days of accrued but untaken annual leaveAny days on which you return to work and perform duties before 15 December, which will be paid at your normal rate.
&nbsp;
Regarding the acting-up allowance, this will be included in your final salary, pro-rated to your last day of employment, as you mentioned below.
&nbsp;
Company equipment
Thank you for confirming that 12 December in the afternoon is suitable for the courier collection; I will arrange this accordingly.

&nbsp;
The temporary withholding of £1,000 is only to ensure the equipment is returned. Provided the courier collects the items on 12 December as arranged, the firm will not withhold the
 amount due to any delay caused by the courier’s delivery timeline.
&nbsp;
Thank you again for bringing these points to our attention. If you need any more clarification or if your fitness to return changes, please let me know, and we will support you accordingly.
&nbsp;
Kind regards,
Natasha
&nbsp;

