March CMC - PDD Trial


As advised in my previous updates, there were various issues that were intended to be dealt with at the March CMC including: Reduction
 of Sample Vehicles, Sample Vehicle Testing, Disclosure and Confidentiality &amp; Information Sharing. I have set out a summary of each of these below:




Reduction of Sample Vehicles





The parties in advance of the CMC had agreed that the Ford Litigation would benefit in reducing its cohort of vehicles. Having considered this carefully with counsel and with our experts
 to ensure that we were ensuring that, even with a reduction of vehicles, the PDD Trial would remain as widely binding and dispositive of the issues as possible, we agreed with the Defendants to reduce the number of Sample Vehicles to be tried at the trial
 from 12 to six. We remain confident that this decision does not impact the prospects of success, and indeed it may actually enhance them as it has meant the parties have been able to perform a sufficient level of testing on the vehicles to best present our
 case to the Court at the PDD Trial.&nbsp;





Sample Vehicle Testing





This was a particularly thorny issue between the parties with agreement being found late in the day on the terms of the order (a copy of which is attached). In essence the Court ordered the
 parties to urgently being to jointly test the vehicles at various test houses across the UK. The Claimants had been pushing for this for a number of months and it was a relief when we finally had this enshrined in an order. A further update on the testing
 we have been undertaking is contained below.





Disclosure





This was the biggest issue between the parties in March. The Defendants, understandably if we were wearing their shoes, did not want to actively participate in the disclosure exercise. They
 argued this was on grounds of proportionality and how much time and money it would cost for them to find documents, however the closer reality is that no Defendant actively wishes to be forced to disclose documents that may be damaging to their case. The parties,
