rewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Monday, September 29, 2025 09:49To:&nbsp;Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Resignation&nbsp;Dear Matt,Further to your resignation on 15 September, I write to remind you of your continuing obligations to Pogust&nbsp;Goodhead during your 3-month notice period.First and foremost, during the balance of your notice period you remain an employee of Pogust&nbsp;Goodhead bound by, &nbsp;inter alia, the following express obligations in your contract of employment with an commencement date of 1 September 2022: clauses 4.2(a),(b), (c), (d), (e) and (f), 4.4, 16 and 17 and the contract addendum dated 12 December 2023.&nbsp;Further, you also remain bound by the implied duty of fidelity to Pogust&nbsp;Goodhead. In short, you have a duty to preserve the relationship of trust and confidence between you and your employer.After the termination date, you remain bound by the confidentiality obligations in clause 16 and the post-termination restrictive covenants in clause 21.&nbsp;Both now and after the termination date where you have signed an undertaking to the Court under any Confidentiality Ring Order you remain, and will remain, bound by that undertaking.Separately, I am aware that you are in discussions with Anna Varga about sending a letter to the client committee on the NOx emissions litigation in which you announce your resignation from Pogust&nbsp;Goodhead, among other matters. Please continue to coordinate with Anna, and do not inform the client committee or any third party (either in writing or orally) that you have resigned from your employment with Pogust&nbsp;Goodhead without written authorisation&nbsp;from Anna. To be clear, this represents a clear management instruction.Thank you for your co-operation.Regards,Raminder&nbsp;​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718&nbsp;"}

