Hi Anna &nbsp;Please see a draft email to counsel below. &nbsp;Jess &nbsp;**********************&nbsp;Ben, Theo, &nbsp;Further to the below, we would like to confirm a few points to ensure we can hit the ground running on your return next week.&nbsp;As per [Anna’s/my] email on Tuesday, you will have seen that the Defendants applications are addressed to both PG, and separately PGMBM Limited, the parent company. Please could you confirm whether you see any difficulty in also being instructed by the parent company in this regard? Any work relating to the parent company would of course be invoiced separately to PGMBM Ltd, rather than apportioned between claimant firms. &nbsp;To recap upcoming deadlines: Evidence in response to the applications is due on 7 November 2025 - we have a draft statement in progress which we hope to be able to share by Monday. The agreed hearing bundle is to be filed on 14 November; skeletons are to be filed and served on 17 November; the agreed bundle of authorities is to be filed on 20 November, ahead of the hearing on 21 November. &nbsp;For ease of reference, we are reattaching the key witness statement from the Defendants’ applications. Please do let us if you have any issues accessing the remaining documents here:  [For Counsel] Funding Disclosure Applications. &nbsp;We would like to schedule a call early next week once you have had a chance to consider the documents – are you available on Monday at 5pm? &nbsp;Kind regards&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;From: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 29 October 2025 09:38To: T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; B.Williams@4newsquare.comCc: Erika Saluzzo &lt;esaluzzo@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Greg Lewis &lt;glewis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Funding disclosure applications&nbsp;Hi Theo, &nbsp;Thank you again for offering to look at this whilst on holida